id: toss
name: Toss
type: standard
actionCost: 1
kiCost: 0
attacking: false
requiresTarget: true
usageLimit: 1/round
# What is tossed asked, at the token targeted; its catcher's Perception Check (Apprentice) from the card's Catch button -
# made, theirs; failed, lost, a Found button for the GM when somebody finds it (chat.mjs askToss, postToss).
toss: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Toss an Item you possess to another Character: an Apprentice Perception Check catches it; failed, it is lost.
text: >
  Toss Maneuver [1/Round]: Give an item to a friend or ally.
  –Maneuver Type: Standard
  –Action Cost: 1 Action
  –KP Cost: N/A
  –Effect: Give a Basic Item, Accessory, Weapon, or piece of Apparel you possess to another Character. That Character must
  make an Apprentice Perception Skill Check. If they succeed, they gain the item. If they fail, it continues sailing past
  them and becomes lost, requiring a Perception Skill Check to find again (with the Difficulty Category decided by the
  ARC depending on the terrain).
